# Native app deploy update message

When you finish **user-visible** changes that will deploy to production (UI, UX, content, fixes to broken flows), update [gospel-admin/data/deploy-update-message.txt](gospel-admin/data/deploy-update-message.txt) so native app users see a short “what changed” note in the restart alert.

## When to update

- **Do update** for changes counselors or counselees might notice.
- **Do not update** for internal-only work (tests, refactors, CI, docs-only, admin tooling with no user impact).
- **Clear the body** (leave only `#` comment lines) when the release has nothing worth telling users.

## Writing rules

- Plain language for app users — not developers.
- No file paths, component names, APIs, “deploy”, “WebView”, “chunk”, or other technical terms.
- **1–3 short sentences** or up to **3 brief bullets**; aim for **~200 characters** (server caps at 400).
- Calm and helpful tone; not marketing hype.

## Examples

- Good: `Fixed an issue where the menu could open an external browser on iPhone.`
- Good: `Daily verse challenge: clearer feedback when you complete a day.`
- Bad: `CapacitorKeepLinksInApp touchstart intercept; router.push for same-origin links.`
- Bad: `Refactored capacitorDeployNotice controller and added Jest mocks.`

## File format

Keep the `#` header comments at the top. Put user-visible text below them (lines starting with `#` are not shown in the app).
